title = "Standard Library Reference"
summary = "Reference documentation for the Caffeine standard library artifacts and types."
---

This page contains the artifacts supported by the current version of the standard library. For an explanation of artifact structure, see the [Documentation](/docs) page.

As of the current version, `SLO` is the only supported artifact in Caffeine's standard library.

***

## SLO - Service Level Objective

### Description

[SLOs](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Service-level_objective) are a very common reliability artifact. This artifact enables users to leverage Caffeine to guide SLO creation, maintenance, and tuning at their engineering organization. In fact,
as noted in [the origin story blog post](/blog/origins), improving the SLO development life cycle ([a concept defined here](https://www.slodlc.com/)) was the motivating factor for Caffeine's creation.

### Definition

*Last modified:* `11/27/25`

```yaml
artifacts:
  - name: SLO
    version: 0.0.1
    base_params:
      threshold: Decimal
      window_in_days: Optional(Integer) -> 30
    params:
      queries: Dict(String, String)
      value: String
```

***